\u2192743\u21921860 (step_02/04/05) \u2014 this is the confound to control for.\n- 1006 has exactly **one** event in the window (step_03): 1006\u21921532, occurring in [37631, 37730] (step_06, step_08, step_14).\n- 1860 has exactly **one** event in the window (step_03): the inbound event 743\u21921860 (step_11), occurring in [36731, 36830] (step_07, step_08, step_15).\n- 1860 has **zero** events anywhere in [36831, 38431] (step_10), and 743\u21921860 never fires after 37631 (step_13).\n\nSo the only event that could deliver influence to 1860 precedes 1006's only outbound event by ~900 time units. The chain runs backwards in time, and no \u2264600-unit hop sequence can bridge it.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_111f4230\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 1532, 1643, 358, 743],\n  \"window\": [36031, 38431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A time-agnostic path 1006->1532->1643->358->743->1860 exists, but it is not time-respecting. 1006 emits its single event (1006->1532) at t in [37631,37730], whereas 1860's single event in the window is the inbound 743->1860 at t in [36731,36830] \u2014 about 900 units earlier. 1860 receives nothing after 36830 and 743->1860 never recurs later, so no chain of hops (each <=600 units) can carry influence from 1006 to 1860. The static connectivity and the moderate activity of hubs 743/1532 are the confounders; both were checked and do not rescue a temporal ordering.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 36834, "total_output_tokens": 6719, "total_tokens": 43553, "total_latency_ms": 94354, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}